{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/service.py:13:deprecated-method"], "search": "    items = [Item.from_orm(r) for r in records]", "replace": "    items = [Item.model_validate(r) for r in records]", "explanation": "`from_orm()` is deprecated in Pydantic v2 (migration.md#changes-to-pydanticbasemodel). Use `model_validate()`, which works on ORM-style objects when the model config sets `from_attributes=True`. That config lives on `Item` in app/models.py, which is outside this edit's scope, so it must be verified there."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/service.py:27:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return json.loads(page_of(items, page).json())", "replace": "    return json.loads(page_of(items, page).model_dump_json())", "explanation": "`.json()` is deprecated; the v2 equivalent is `model_dump_json()` (migration.md#changes-to-pydanticbasemodel table). `json.loads` of its output keeps the same result."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/service.py:31:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return item.copy(update={"stock": item.stock + amount})", "replace": "    return item.model_copy(update={"stock": item.stock + amount})", "explanation": "`.copy()` is deprecated; the v2 equivalent is `model_copy()` (migration.md#changes-to-pydanticbasemodel table). The `update=` argument behaves the same way."}], "notes": "Three edits address the three findings in app/service.py. Each search string is a single line that occurs exactly once. No imports need changing: `json`, `List`, `LRU`, `Item`, `Page`, and `Settings` are all still used.

Not changed: `cache_snapshot()` calls `_cache.copy().dict()`. `_cache` is an `LRU` from app/cache.py, not a Pydantic model, and no finding covers it. Leaving it alone follows the rule to change only what the findings require.

Dependency outside this file: the `Item.model_validate(r)` change only works on ORM-style objects if `Item` sets `model_config = ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)` (or the equivalent) in app/models.py. That file is migrated separately and was not edited here, so confirm it there. If it is missing, `load_items` will fail for non-dict inputs."}
